  "title": "We Three Kings",
  "composer": "John Henry Hopkins Jr.",
  "about": "John Henry Hopkins Jr., an American clergyman and hymn writer, wrote this carol in 1857 for a Christmas pageant at the seminary where he taught. Its original title is Three Kings of Orient, and it was published in 1863. The carol tells of the Magi of the Bible, who brought gold, frankincense and myrrh. Its verse is in a minor key, and the refrain turns to the major.",
  "funFact": "Hopkins planned the carol so that three men each sing one verse alone, one for each king.",
